      "id": 1,
      "text": "Iota earned its name when the Southern Pacific Railroad built a depot near the old Cartville settlement, naming the stop Iota.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iota%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "C.C. Duson founded Iota in 1894, buying 160 acres and laying out town lots that attracted early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iota%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Acadia Canal lifted water 29 feet via flumes, irrigating up to 2,000 acres by 1901 and spurring rice farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/iota_louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pointe-aux-Loups mineral springs drew visitors from 1858, making the area one of Acadia Parish’s oldest attraction sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iota%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every year, Iota hosts the Tee Mamou‑Iota Mardi Gras Folklife Festival, where riders on horseback collect gumbo ingredients.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/iota_louisiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Iota officially incorporated in 1901 under the Lawrason Act, becoming a formal town within the Crowley Micropolitan area.",
